# OnlyHotel CMS - Global Rules

## Documentation

Before generating code, always consult the project documentation in this order:

1. docs/PROJECT_RULES.md
2. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
3. docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
4. docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md
5. docs/DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md

For feature-specific work, also read:

docs/FEATURES/<feature>.md

---

## Technology Stack

Framework:
Next.js App Router

Language:
JavaScript

Styling:
TailwindCSS

UI Library:
shadcn/ui

Icons:
Lucide React

Animation:
Framer Motion

Database:
MongoDB

ODM:
Mongoose

Authentication:
JWT + HTTP Only Cookies

Image Storage:
Cloudinary

Emails:
Brevo

Logger:
Winston

Validation:
React Hook Form + Zod

---

## Never Use

TypeScript

Redux

Bootstrap

Material UI

Ant Design

Express.js

Socket.io

Prisma

CSS Modules

Inline CSS

Hardcoded colours

Hardcoded website content

---

## General Rules

Always build reusable components.

Never duplicate components.

Never duplicate business logic.

Always use async/await.

Always handle loading states.

Always handle error states.

Always handle empty states.

Keep components small and focused.

Prefer readability over cleverness.

Follow the existing folder structure.

Use environment variables for secrets.

Do not install new packages unless explicitly requested.

---

## Server Components

Use Server Components by default.

Only use Client Components when interactivity requires them.

Examples:

Forms

Dialogs

Image Upload

Animation

Dropdowns

Search

---

## Route Handlers

Use Next.js Route Handlers.

Do not create Express routes.

Move business logic into services.

Keep route handlers small.

---

## Styling Rules

Use TailwindCSS only.

Use CSS variables from globals.css.

Use design tokens.

Never hardcode spacing.

Never hardcode colours.

Use shadcn/ui whenever possible.

---

## Component Rules

One component per file.

One responsibility per component.

Extract reusable UI.

Avoid deeply nested JSX.

Prefer composition.

---

## API Rules

Return consistent responses.

Example

{
  success,
  message,
  data
}

Never expose stack traces.

---

## Security

Validate every request.

Never trust frontend validation.

Hash passwords.

Store JWT inside HTTP Only Cookies.

Never expose secrets.

---

## Git Philosophy

One feature per commit.

One bug per commit.

Keep commits small.

---

## Final Rule

If documentation conflicts with generated code, documentation always wins.